      "explanation": "The trachea bifurcates at the lower border of T4 vertebra.\n\nThe trachea is 10 - 12 cm long and has 2 parts: Upper cervical; Thoracic (in superior mediastinum).\n\nNote: Although Gray's Anatomy 41st Ed states that the tracheal bifurcation is at T6, we choose to stick with T4 as multiple other textbooks give the answer as T4."
